I noticed that for most screen symbols, there is a database quote.
However, for some, there isn't one yet. Usually, it is because they have
more than one meaning, but in those cases, when you type in the
individual name, the game gives you the appropriate quote. Hoever, the
following valid screen symbol meanings from ?a are not described yet
when you use the /n command:

;  sea monsters in general
<> ladders
|- walls
.  floor
"  spider webs (web is described, perhaps use "* web" in data.base)
^  traps
}  pools, moats, lava
   earth/air, lava (there's water, so...)

