Also, if I ask information (with /) on the / symbol, I get "a wand or a
wall". I don't recall having seen / walls before, and if they do exist,
I suppose that \ can also be a wall, which isn't mentioned with that
symbol (it's only a throne). Also, / is not mentioned in the ?a help as
a wall.

In that /a command, <> aren't mentioned as ladders, while | and - are
mentioned only as "a wall", while they could also be a hidden door
(undiscovered). Since the ^ description is "A trap (once you detect
it).", I think that the secret door should be mentioned somewhere as
well. The | and - symbols seem appropriate: "A wall or (undiscovered)
secret door".

The same, by the way, would be valid for the space character: next to "a
ghost or dark part of a room or air", it can also be a secret door (at
the end of a corridor).

Even more obscure, the . character might also be an as yet undiscovered
magic portal... Including it in the help file may just be the hint a
player needs to decipher the cryptic message of the Quest leader (after
all he tells you to *look* for a magic portal, not to *search* for it).

And why is the description of the + character "... or a spellbook
containing a spell you can learn." ? The ?/! descriptions don't mention
that you can "read", "zap" or "quaff" them either...

